Subject: Fix build with glibc 2.34+ (non-constant SIGSTKSZ)

glibc 2.34 turned SIGSTKSZ into a non-constant macro
(defined as sysconf(_SC_SIGSTKSZ)), which breaks the
preprocessor expression `SIGSTKSZ < 16384` in c-stack.c.

Drop the compile-time size comparison so the code builds
against both old and new glibc; the libsigsegv workaround
(redefining SIGSTKSZ to 16384) is still applied whenever
libsigsegv is available.

--- a/lib/c-stack.c
+++ b/lib/c-stack.c
@@ -53,3 +53,3 @@
 #ifndef SIGSTKSZ
 # define SIGSTKSZ 16384
-#elif HAVE_LIBSIGSEGV && SIGSTKSZ < 16384
+#elif HAVE_LIBSIGSEGV
